    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d594">

                <pb facs="0763" n="689" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg689"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.85/106</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Siam</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Arnold</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-13T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 13, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your August 7, 10 a.m.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d594-f1"/> Telegraph exact status of
                    situation. American Government desires to be considered in any apportionment of
                    these steamers and you will so notify Siamese Government. Department understands
                    that it is proposed to allot 35 per cent to the British, a similar amount to the
                    French, and 30 per cent to the Japanese, with the understanding that the latter
                    will utilize the tonnage or its equivalent in relieving the war needs of the
                    Allies, to which restriction the Japanese object. American Government especially
                    anxious to share in the distribution of this tonnage and you will keep
                    Department informed of any developments that may give this Government
                    opportunity to participate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
